{"availability":"available","full":"Camilu-png/pixel-crochet","name":"pixel-crochet","description":"Nobody picks up a crochet hook to do math. Pixel Crochet does the counting for you.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-28T02:47:28Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:38:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pixel-crochet.vercel.app","topics":["crochet","crochet-tracker"],"demo":"https://pixel-crochet.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.774Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.774Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.774Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.774Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nobody picks up a crochet hook to do math. Pixel Crochet does the counting for you.","Pixel Crochet is a free, open-source app for tapestry crochet that takes the hardest part — keeping count — and turns it into something you barely notice. Paste a Stitch Fiddle–style pattern, or import a picture of pixel art or cross-stitch, and the app builds an interactive guide. Follow it row by row, tap the blocks you finish, and your progress saves itself.","Tapestry crochet is perfect until row 47 of 213. Then you lose your place, squint at the tiny numbers, count for the fourth time, and quietly accept that the row has to be undone."],"features":["Import a picture, wear the pattern later. Drop a PNG or JPG of pixel art or cross-stitch and the app turns it into a pattern: it detects the color palette, suggests stitch dimensions, and lets you swap any color for the…","Paste or upload Stitch Fiddle patterns. Text patterns in the standard Row N: 10 red, 5 white format are parsed for you — paste the text or pick a .txt file.","A guide, not a wall of numbers. The current row is split into color blocks, with an arrow that respects the reading direction (left-to-right or right-to-left) — that detail that ends more projects than it should.","Progress with a tap. Finish a block, tap it, done — it's crossed out. Realized you miscounted? Step back a row, or jump anywhere in the pattern.","Saved on autopilot. Close the app at midnight; next evening it opens exactly where you left off. No exporting, no printing, no remembering."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Camilu-png/pixel-crochet/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bfcfbc29666e2a652552d8dbbe164237b7b4bdbad6a7ead436338dbffc9159d6","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.968Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.968Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Nobody picks up a crochet hook to do math. Pixel Crochet does the counting for you.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Camilu-png/pixel-crochet/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"bfcfbc29666e2a652552d8dbbe164237b7b4bdbad6a7ead436338dbffc9159d6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Camilu-png/pixel-crochet/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.968Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T21:38:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Camilu-png/pixel-crochet/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.969Z","hash":"bfcfbc29666e2a652552d8dbbe164237b7b4bdbad6a7ead436338dbffc9159d6","originalBytes":5147,"storedBytes":5147,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["crochet","pixel","row","stitch","flutter","pattern","app","patterns","import","paste","text","blocks","color","image","made","project","tapestry","features","fiddle","follow","step","what","who","art","count","counting","cross-stitch","current","dimensions","direction","english","example","file","finish","free","generated","guide","home","how","i18n","interactive","jpg","keep","lib","license","localizations","love","mark","one","pick","picture","png","progress","run","shared","stitch.","suggest","support","tap","test","turns","txt","while","yarn","about","accept","across","actually","advance","alive.","always","amarilla.txt","an